{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b> [לכן] — twice at the beginning of a parashah: here and the other לכן אמור לבני ישראל (Leviticus 17:12). This is what HaShem said in Egypt: 'A locked garden is My sister, My bride' — and now you are near the land, and you are breached in forbidden relations:" "<b>Therefore</b> [לכן] — in gematria: measure for measure." "<b>My covenant of peace</b> — שלם [שלום] is written [defective, without the vav], and it is the וי״ו קטיעא [the severed/cut vav] in chapter 83 of Kiddushin, when it is whole. Another interpretation: a complete gift I give him — 10 gifts in the Temple, 10 in the province (for יו״ד in plene = כ׳ in gematria). Another interpretation: the cut vav, because Pinchas is Elijah, and so אליה is written defective [without the vav], and יעקוב is written plene [with vav] — he took the vav from Elijah as a pledge until he comes with the Messiah and redeems his sons, and this is 'יגל יעקב ישמח ישראל ישמח' — the letters of משיח [in] 'ישמח' — he will rejoice in the days of the Messiah, and the vav will return, and Elijah will be whole:" "<b>Peace</b> [שלום] — in gematria this is משיח." "<b>Shelumiel</b> [שלומיאל] — in gematria this is Zimri son of Salu [זמרי בן סלוא]."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase גן נעול אחותי כלה quotes Song of Songs 4:12. The second לכן at the head of a parashah is at Leviticus 17:12."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:14.187675047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}